    <name>
      <text>Simplifying using laws of logarithms</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify the following expression using the laws of logarithms:</p>

<p>\(\log_{@b@}({@m@})+\log_{@b@}({@n@})\)</p>

<p>Enter your final numerical answer below.</p>

<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Recall the product law of logarithms:</p>

<p>\(\log_b(m)+\log_b(n)=\log_b(mn)\).</p>

<p>Since \(m=b^p\) and \(n=b^q\), we have</p>

<p>\(\log_b(m)=\log_b(b^p)=p\)</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>\(\log_b(n)=\log_b(b^q)=q\).</p>

<p>Therefore,</p>

<p>\(\log_b(m)+\log_b(n)=p+q={@ans@}.\)</p>

<p>Hence, the correct answer is <m>{@ans@}</m>.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
